messages:
anya: Saw a weird pattern on /pricing: people hover the calculator area a lot but abandon. Heatmap: https://redwood-internal/hm/50321. Thinking a micro-offer that ties into the webinar copy and routes intented leads.

rachel: Paste the core metrics?

anya: impressions 3.6k, calc CTA CTR 1.4%, hover-to-click ~14:1, median dwell 3.9s. Top FAQ question 'what affects price' expands 27%. Many users re-open the calc.

tom: Hypothesis: users want reassurance about cost drivers. Proposal: two-step microflow inside the calc: 1) after second hover >2s show a small pill: "See cost at your scale (2 options)" 2) choices: "Quick snapshot" or "Join pricing mini-workshop". Keep form tiny: email + company size.

analytics-bot: Events to implement: rw_calc_pill_shown, rw_calc_choice, rw_calc_submit. Capture calc_session_id, page_variant, logged_in_email if present.

sales-ops: Routing idea: if choice=="mini-workshop" AND company_size>=200 OR utm_campaign contains "enterprise_launch", route to SDR queue "pricing-hot" (24h SLA). If snapshot chosen, send automated snapshot email and add to nurture. Tag leads with variant and calc_session_id.

rachel: For copy, avoid heavy words. Draft A: "Reserve a 25-min pricing mini-workshop  practical setup + Q&A" CTA: "Reserve". Draft B: "Get a quick cost snapshot for your workload" CTA: "Get snapshot". Also add a one-line FAQ link: "What influences cost most?" that anchors into FAQ.

tom: I'll wire GTM names: rw_pill_show, rw_choice_click, rw_submit. Snippet for HubSpot routing (sales-ops):
```
if (lead.choice == 'mini-workshop' && lead.company_size >= 200) {
  assignQueue('pricing-hot');
  setSLA(24);
} else if (lead.choice == 'snapshot') {
  sendAutomatedSnapshot();
  addToNurture('pricing_snapshot_flow');
}
```

sales-ops: Will build workflow. One Q: what SLA for pricing-hot? 24h ok. Also want variant token in SDR message template to personalize outreach.

anya: 24h SLA fine. Action items: rachel  finalize two micro-copy variants + FAQ anchor by 4pm. tom  add GTM events + dashboard by EOD tomorrow. sales-ops  HubSpot workflow + templates + SLA by tomorrow noon. analytics-bot  confirm payload includes calc_session_id + email when authenticated. I'll draft the webinar blurb to mirror the mini-workshop (3 bullets: cost levers, batching & quantization benefits, deployment options) and drop in #marketing for review. :sparkles:
